)ATTR DEFAULT(@}_)
 @ TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE)
 } TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN)
 { TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(TURQ)
 _ TYPE(INPUT)  INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(RED)    CAPS(ON) JUST(LEFT)
 ! TYPE(OUTPUT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) CAPS(OFF) JUST(LEFT)
)BODY
@HELP: DA Panel -- Fields                       !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                   }
}
{  JOBNAME  }The name of the job, started task, TSO user or initiator.
{  STEPNAME }The step running, for a batch job; the procedure of a
}            started task; the logon procedure of a TSO user.
{  PROCSTEP }The step of the procedure; for a TSO user, the terminal.
{  TYPE     }JOB, STC or TSU; blank for an idle initiator.
{  JNUM     }The JES2 job number, if the address space has one.
{  C        }The job class.
{  POS      }IN in storage, OUT swapped out, N/S not swappable.
{  DP       }The dispatching priority, in hexadecimal.
{  PGN      }The performance group. Overtype it to move the address space
}            to another one: a RESET (E name,PERFORM=n). It needs update
}            access to the job, or to SDSF.OPER for one without a job.
{  REAL     }The frames of real storage it holds.
{  PAGING   }Not measured yet: always 0.00.
{  SIO      }The I/O (EXCPs) per second since the panel was last shown.
{  CPU%     }The share of the processor since the panel was last shown.
}
}  SIO and CPU% are taken over the time between two displays: the first
}  display shows 0.00, Enter shows the next interval. PF11 shows further
}  fields (next topic).
}  Enter: next topic   PF7: DA panel help   PF3: back to SDSF
)PROC
  &ISFHPFK = .PFKEY
  &ZCONT = ISFHDAF2
  &ZUP = ISFHDA
)END
